ncontract: weighted deformed attachment point and orientation must transform\nunder a common superposed rigid rotation, with the existing linearized weights\nand exact direct/identical-rotation limit. If weighted-rotation-vector averaging\nis confirmed responsible, propose an objective SO(3) mean and its connected\nkinematic map/Jacobian/geometric tangent/rotation-force covector treatment at the\nearly checkpoint. An objective mean may replace the nonobjective average on the\nnew active rotating-offset route, including slave orientation if necessary;\nthe small-rotation/public linearized relation stays compatible. Account for\ninverse restart mapping, constraint postchecks and any downstream nonlinear\nrotation dependency refusals. Do not simply rotate an offset objectively while\nleaving a nonobjective beam orientation and then claim wrench/objectivity pass.\nThis is candidate design within adopted objective; Astra reviews scientific\napplicability. Do not expand zero-offset legacy capability or arbitrary chart\ncrossing claims, alter physical material laws, or fit the analytical reference.\n\n4. Close accepted-state test gaps from supervisor_dc_review.md: every accepted\nsnapshot copied-state residual<=1e-7 at ACHIEVED lambda, constraints/reactions,\nno reconstruction mutation; full final and milestone GP/fiber material histories\nfull vs resumed at EXISTING tolerances, not scalar alpha maxima alone; snapshots\nretain accepted history after later trials; caller-owned inputs observed and\nunchanged on rejection and cancellation. Match adaptive physical milestones,\nnot an assumed exactly6 accepted increments. No empty conditional passes.\n\n## Resource and handoff\n\nBudget used1486.0224586999684/3600; remaining2113.9775413000316 including900 final\nreserve. THIS assignment permits at most450 ADDITIONAL process-wall seconds for\nproduct numerical checks through harness (shared ledger, not renewed authority),\nleaving independent mesh/arc and final verification capacity. No allow-reserve.\nPer diagnostic120s; pytest regression may up to600 only if remaining assignment\nand task allowance permit. One numerical child. Every fail/timeout counts.\nDo not run mesh/arc/final25. Do not rerun unchanged source16. Use cached immutable\nsolves and discriminating focused checks; preserve all failures. Once450 spent,\ncontinue nonnumerical fixes/doc and handoff without more solves. Need more\nexecution? Report exact unresolved question and evidence, do not silently renew.\n\nCheckpoint reports findings, intended edit, source/test changes, actual checks,\nremaining work/budget and reserved choices. Final handoff must label partial,\nimplemented-unverified or verified; exact files, outcomes, counts, failures,\nevidence paths and numerical cost. Update living HANDOVER.md actual facts only.\n", "numLines": 83, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "83 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\.development\\nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\\SLICE3_UNBLOCK_DELIVERY.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "effect-9052ae39-b605-5ea8-963f-b9b950362c30", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349473096, "updatedAt": 1792349473152, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:\\Users\\AudunArnesenNyhus\\.codex\\AGENTS.md", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:\\Users\\AudunArnesenNyhus\\.codex\\AGENTS.md", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:\\Users\\AudunArnesenNyhus\\.codex\\AGENTS.md", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Users\\AudunArnesenNyhus\\.codex\\AGENTS.md", "offset": null, "limit": 2000}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Users\\AudunArnesenNyhus\\.codex\\AGENTS.md", "content": "# Working preferences\n\n- Complete authorised implementation, verification and handoff. Make reasonable reversible choices; ask only when missing information changes correctness, scope or external consequences. Investigation alone does not authorise fixes. Existing approval remains valid within its scope, including routine disposable checks and their repair.\n- Follow the current request and repository contract. Historical plans are evidence, not active authority. Keep repository-specific engineering, qualification, resource and release rules in their repositories; keep shared worker policy here. Global guidance and skills must not weaken repository gates, add unrelated work or reuse consumed authority.\n- Read only needed symbols, ranges and guidance; batch independent reads. Keep full diagnostics on disk and report counts, failures and paths. Estimate broad output before printing; avoid full catalogs, large arrays and encoded media. Read `~/.codex/harness/README.md` only when its optional helpers are needed.\n- Verify proportionately and meet required gates. Check effective runtime settings before claiming a configuration works. Repeat passed checks only for changed inputs, failures or unresolved concerns. Preserve failed evidence, scientific tolerances and independent reviews; distinguish implementation, testing, acceptance and release. Never claim unmeasured savings.\n- Use bounded waits and compact status checks; checkpoint work spanning turns. On pause, launch no new work, stop only owned activity as requested and save minimum restart state. Create user-visible tasks only when requested.\n- Lead with the result in concise plain language. Report meaningful changes, evidence and blockers; avoid repeated status and ritual approvals.\n\n# Model roles and ownership\n\nAstra uses the configured OpenAI model and owns decomposition, repository selection, architecture and contract decisions, worker authority, verification, reconciliation, integration, Git delivery and final acceptance. Honour explicit model/effort choices.\n\n| Level | Default responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| Local OpenCode | Short, tightly specified lookups, evidence extraction, documentation, mechanical edits and simple checks within demonstrated capability. |\n| Mistral | Default owner of substantial bounded implementation milestones: investigation, candidate design, central algorithm, connected integration, debugging, focused verification, repair, documentation and handoff. Independent review of other authors when useful. |\n| OpenAI | Orchestration, architecture, governing contracts, unresolved high-consequence reasoning, scientific adjudication, cross-repository integration and final acceptance; direct implementation when coupling, confidentiality or availability warrants it. |\n\nBounded multiagent workflows are welcome when specialization, implementation capacity or independent review adds value. Astra may delegate autonomously within authorised scope. Use the lowest suitable level; dispatch suitable substantial work directly to Mistral without a prerequisite local attempt. Avoid Mistral overhead for trivial work, duplicate investigations, overlapping writes, full-history forks and delegation merely to create activity. Keep tightly coupled work with one owner; independent work may proceed concurrently within shared resource limits.\n\nFor substantial implementation, assign Mistral the largest coherent outcome fitting established contracts and budgets, including its central algorithm and integration. Do not routinely keep coding with Astra while assigning Mistral only helper work, tests or documentation. Numerical difficulty alone does not reserve implementation for Astra. Mistral may inspect and plan the route, propose alternatives, derive candidate equations, choose compatible internal algorithms/data layouts, simplify duplicate services, build verification tools and repair its owned code and harness.\n\nThis applies across the ANY ecosystem to complete solver, mechanics, meshing, geometry, application and tooling subsystems: static/transient and nonlinear routes, enforcement/contact/history, materials/elements, assembly and operators, retained-coordinate/dynamics mechanics, geometry/event control, state/restart/rollback, public APIs/persistence/results, shared-service refactoring, benchmark/reference tooling, CI/build/install workflows and measured performance/correctness repair. Repository ownership and execution authority remain explicit; eligibility grants no sibling edits, qualification campaigns or publication.\n\nAstra supplies governing contracts and adopts changes to physical assumptions, public compatibility, architecture boundaries, scientific tolerances, capability claims or execution authority. Workers may propose changes with evidence but may not adopt reserved changes unilaterally. Resolve concrete boundaries with a concise delta and let the same owner finish. Prefer useful delivered outcomes over worker quotas or approval ceremonies. If Astra implements directly while Mistral is available, briefly record the concrete coupling, confidentiality or reserved-decision reason in the existing task note. Apply ownership changes prospectively; do not restart completed work to change its author.\n\n# Assignment, communication and completion\n\n- Determine the repository from the request, checkout, remotes and project context; pass its absolute root. Read permits investigation, planning or review without edits; Edit permits expressly authorised implementation, tests or documentation.\n- Before Edit dispatch, inspect enough context to preserve dirty work and concurrent ownership. Give one outcome-oriented brief: repository, mode, owned files/subsystem, objective, essential context, governing contracts and task-specific invariants, protected evidence, shared resource limits, permitted checks and acceptance/handoff criteria. Allow new files only within the owned boundary; cross-repository work needs separately authorised ownership.\n- Authorise the connected inspect/design/implement/debug/check/repair/document loop within that boundary. Permit ordinary reversible decisions, impact-based check selection and repair of permitted failures without serial permission requests. Escalate concrete contract, ownership, authority or resource boundaries. Workers must not launch workers, broaden ownership or consume additional authority. Delegation never multiplies numerical budgets or renews frozen authority.\n- Workers must not commit, push, change branches/history, reset/discard work, edit other repositories or alter unrelated configuration unless Astra explicitly grants that authority. Astra owns Git integration and publication.\n- Keep coordination compact: send only scope, objective, authority, essential context and criteria; reference artifacts instead of repeating history/logs. Batch related messages, use deltas on follow-up and avoid routine acknowledgements/status. Reports contain outcome, changed files, checks actually run, actionable findings, blockers and evidence paths. Keep full diagnostics on disk; preserve uncertainty and failed evidence.\n- For substantial Edit assignments, include one early progress checkpoint before inspection consumes most of the turn budget: concrete findings, intended edit, remaining work and blockers. Use a compact artifact or report, not a permission gate. Set a checkpoint deadline appropriate to the assignment. At that point Astra inspects actual artifacts and remaining implementation/check/handoff work using a compact status read, not repeated polling. If the checkpoint is missing or investigation dominates, inspect the cause and supply missing context, narrow the deliverable or stop a demonstrably stalled owned run; do not wait blindly for the turn limit. Let the owner choose internal sequencing and compatible methods within its scope.\r\n- Give every Mistral Edit assignment a realistic turn budget and explicit completion requirements. Reserve the final turns for focused verification and handoff. Before exhausting the limit, save a concise checkpoint at an explicitly permitted evidence path or designated task note (use the final response if file permissions prevent saving): changed files, completed checks, failures, remaining work, unresolved decisions and evidence paths. Label handoff state as inspection only, partial implementation, implemented but unverified, or verified against assigned criteria, with evidence and remaining gaps. Worker verification does not establish final acceptance; never claim checks that did not run.\n- For resource-bounded checks, use a small execution harness that records the exact command, input/candidate identity, effective runtime, exit or timeout status, precise process-wall duration, cumulative budget used and remaining, counts, full stdout/stderr and machine-readable results when supported. Use unique evidence paths for each attempt; preserve failures and partial timeout output. Bound each process-tree timeout by the remaining authorised check budget, retaining any integration/verification reserve. Do not substitute pytest-reported duration or rounded shell seconds for required process-wall accounting. If accounting is missing, recover existing evidence and report uncertainty; do not rerun to reconstruct it or assume authority remains. This adds no numerical execution authority or acceptance gate.\r\n- A limit-reached run or missing handoff is incomplete unless inspected evidence satisfies the task. Inspect partial artifacts and remaining execution authority before a focused continuation; return actionable findings to the same owner with a delta brief when available. If required verification cannot fit the remaining budget, preserve the candidate and report the unmet gate; do not waive checks or renew authority. Continue the same owner from useful artifacts with missing context or actionable findings; a turn limit alone does not justify takeover. Astra takes over when execution is unreliable, the owner is unavailable, or a concrete coupling, confidentiality or reserved-decision boundary requires it; record the reason briefly. Narrow work after repeated unfinished runs; extend turn limits only for demonstrated progress within remaining authority, preserving prior failures and required checks. Classify service failure, intentional interruption, turn exhaustion, implementation defects and verification-evidence gaps separately; absent checks are not disobedience when execution was prohibited. If interrupted before checkpointing, Astra preserves the logs and reconstructs actual progress. Limits are execution bounds, not guaranteed token caps.\n\n# Worker entry points\n\nUse the wrappers (PowerShell 7):\n\n```powershell\n& \"$HOME\\bin\\mistral-worker.ps1\" `\n    -Repo \"<absolute repository root>\" -Mode <Read|Edit> `\n    -Task \"<bounded outcome, ownership and contracts>\" -MaxTurns <N>\n\n& \"$HOME\\bin\\opencode-worker.ps1\" `\n    -Repo \"<absolute repository root>\" -Mode <Read|Edit> `\n    -Task \"<bounded task>\" -MaxSteps <N> -TimeoutSeconds <N>\n```\n\nOmit local `-Model` for the configured default, or supply `-Model \"<configured local provider/model>\"`; do not hard-code today's model into policy. Do not download models, reconfigure the server or switch local-only data to cloud inference without authorisation. Follow each wrapper's actual permission contract.\n\nThe local wrapper supports configured OpenAI-compatible loopback HTTP(S) providers, pins worker/helper inference to the selected model and disables sharing/external plugins. Its application permissions are not an OS sandbox or complete network isolation. Read denies edits; both modes deny unlisted tools/commands, nested workers, network tools and external directories except OpenCode's internal tool-output directory. Environment-file protections remain intact; Edit permits only owned repository edits.\n\nThe default shell allowlist contains specific Git inspections. Add `-AllowedCommands @('<exact authorised command>')` only for needed Read inspections or relevant Edit checks; never bypass failures with arbitrary interpreters, shell composition, wildcards or Git integration commands. Logs stay outside repositories; local `-OutputDirectory` selects a new evidence directory.\n\nQueue short local jobs through the wrapper's shared local-server slot. `-QueueWaitSeconds` bounds waiting separately (default 15 seconds; 0 for immediate fallback); `-TimeoutSeconds` starts when the process launches after acquiring the slot. `LOCAL_QUEUE_BUSY` means no inference started: use suitable Mistral/OpenAI when waiting would delay delivery, respecting local-only constraints, or defer. Queue records preserve wait/execution timing. This coordinates cooperating wrappers, not direct Ollama clients; do not bypass the queue or repeatedly retry a busy slot. Prefer short local jobs over long audits. Use proportionate Mistral `MaxTurns`, local agent `MaxSteps` and local process-tree `TimeoutSeconds`.\n\n# Availability and fallback\n\nLocal models and Mistral are optional dependencies. Local services/models/hardware/tools may be unavailable or unreliable; Mistral may have startup, authentication, transport, context, inference, rate-limit or allowance failures. Treat exhausted Mistral usage as unavailable for the current task.\n\nCheck availability only when useful, using one small bounded Read task through the wrapper and inspecting successful tool outcomes. A launcher, running service, CLI version, plausible answer or zero exit code alone is insufficient. Reuse established availability; do not probe before every assignment. Retain cached unavailability/exhaustion for the current task until new evidence warrants a useful attempt; do not repeatedly retry the same failure or probe unrelated workers.\n\nIf local is unavailable, use suitable Mistral/OpenAI; if Mistral is unavailable, use OpenAI; if both are unavailable, Astra continues directly. Preserve useful partial work and failed evidence. Optional workers must not block delivery or silently relax local-only constraints. Report availability when it affects the requested workflow, confidence, scope or timing. Identify any required local or independent gate left unmet; fallback does not establish different-family independence.\n\n# Verification and acceptance\n\nAfter every Edit worker, inspect Git status/diff, confirm ownership and preserved dirty work, independently run or inspect relevant checks, and resolve unexpected changes or failures. For behavior-changing repairs, confirm regression coverage of the affected contracts, including refusal, mutation and cancellation paths where relevant; add focused tests when existing coverage is insufficient. Helpers alone do not prove caller or production-path integration. Require evidence for important test-pass claims. Check consequential Read findings against source, data, equations or runtime state. For local runs, inspect effective model routing, permissions/steps and actual tool outcomes in saved logs.\n\nFor useful independent review of consequential OpenAI implementation, numerics, mechanics contracts or difficult debugging, prefer an available Mistral Read reviewer; a suitable local model may provide supporting independent input. Prefer different model families; OpenCode is a runner, not a family. Give the artifact and question without Astra's preferred answer unless that answer is under review. Seek errors, counterexamples, unsupported assumptions and missing tests; review complete slices with evidence rather than redundant/trivial fragments. An implementation author cannot supply its sole required independent assessment.\n\nResolve disagreement through underlying evidence and a discriminating check when practical. Preserve scientific gates, physical assumptions, tolerances, failed evidence, consumed authority, release restrictions and unresolved uncertainty. Worker reports and model agreement are evidence, not acceptance; Astra owns final acceptance and user-facing handoff.\r\n", "numLines": 76, "startLine": 1, "requestedOffset": null, "requestedLimit": 2000, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": false}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "76 lines from C:\\Users\\AudunArnesenNyhus\\.codex\\AGENTS.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
