{"id": "effect-f7d63533-2ec6-5bac-a7e6-0712d82da081", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349552383, "updatedAt": 1792349552417, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\nonlinear_state.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\nonlinear_state.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\nonlinear_state.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\nonlinear_state.py", "offset": 1422, "limit": 80}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\nonlinear_state.py", "content": "        self,\r\n        *,\r\n        full_displacement: Any = None,\r\n        full_coordinates: Any = None,\r\n    ) -> StateTrialToken:\r\n        with self._lock:\r\n            if self._active_token is not None:\r\n                raise StateTransactionError(\"A nonlinear-state trial is already active\")\r\n            if self._native_rotation_store is not None and (\r\n                full_displacement is None or full_coordinates is None\r\n            ):\r\n                raise StateTransactionError(\r\n                    \"Native nonlinear-state trials require the complete global \"\r\n                    \"displacement and nodal-coordinate arrays\"\r\n                )\r\n            self._serial += 1\r\n            token = StateTrialToken(self._generation, self._serial, self._owner)\r\n            child_tokens: Dict[Hashable, StateTrialToken] = {}\r\n            native_token: Optional[NativeRotationTrialToken] = None\r\n            try:\r\n                for key, batch in self._batches.items():\r\n                    child_tokens[key] = batch.begin_trial()\r\n                if self._native_rotation_store is not None:\r\n                    native_token = self._native_rotation_store.begin_trial(\r\n                        full_displacement,\r\n                        full_coordinates,\r\n                    )\r\n            except Exception:\r\n                for key, child_token in child_tokens.items():\r\n                    self._batches[key].discard_trial(child_token)\r\n                if (\r\n                    self._native_rotation_store is not None\r\n                    and native_token is not None\r\n                ):\r\n                    self._native_rotation_store.discard_trial(native_token)\r\n                raise\r\n            self._batch_trial_tokens = child_tokens\r\n            self._native_rotation_trial_token = native_token\r\n            self._native_trial_full_displacement = (\r\n                None\r\n                if native_token is None\r\n                else np.frombuffer(\r\n                    np.ascontiguousarray(\r\n                        np.asarray(full_displacement, dtype=np.float64)\r\n                    ).tobytes(order=\"C\"),\r\n                    dtype=np.float64,\r\n                ).reshape(np.asarray(full_displacement).shape)\r\n            )\r\n            self._fallback_trial = {}\r\n            self._active_token = token\r\n            return token\r\n\r\n    def begin(\r\n        self,\r\n        *,\r\n        full_displacement: Any = None,\r\n        full_coordinates: Any = None,\r\n    ) -> StateTrialToken:\r\n        \"\"\"Short transaction alias for :meth:`begin_trial`.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n        return self.begin_trial(\r\n            full_displacement=full_displacement,\r\n            full_coordinates=full_coordinates,\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def active_trial_token(self) -> StateTrialToken:\r\n        \"\"\"Return the active token for an assembly evaluator.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n        with self._lock:\r\n            if self._active_token is None:\r\n                raise StateTransactionError(\"No nonlinear-state trial is active\")\r\n            return self._active_token\r\n\r\n    def replace_trial(\r\n        self,\r\n        *,\r\n        full_displacement: Any = None,\r\n        full_coordinates: Any = None,\r\n    ) -> StateTrialToken:\r\n        \"\"\"Reject any prior candidate and begin another from committed state.\"\"\"\r\n", "numLines": 80, "startLine": 1422, "requestedOffset": 1422, "requestedLimit": 80, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "80 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\src\\anysolver\\nonlinear_state.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-2040e623-1840-5871-9ce0-c13f15d3e302-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349555593, "updatedAt": 1792349555593, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Critical: `begin_trial` raises `StateTransactionError(\"A nonlinear-state trial is already active\")` if a trial is active. So inside the Newton loop, after the iteration's assembly created an active trial, a line-search assembly would raise unless the current trial is discarded first.\n\nSo the line search must: discard the current active trial (it belongs to a non-converged iterate and won't be committed), then for each alpha: assemble (creates trial), evaluate, discard. After the line search, the loop continues to the next iteration which assembles fresh. But careful: `states_new` variable — on the delta path, states_new isn't used (only set on convergence break). But `states_new = committed_states` is initialized at attempt start; if the attempt later converges at iteration k, states_new = trial_states of that iteration. The line search at iteration j<k discards trials — fine since those iterates were never accepted.\n\nBut wait — is the persistent store even in use for these tests? `finish_state_evaluation`: if committed_states is not a NonlinearStateStore (legacy dict), trials are just fresh dicts, no active-trial concept, discard is a no-op. The EP tests likely use the legacy path or the store depending on config. Either way, discarding before each line-search assembly handles both: for the store, discard the active trial first; for legacy dicts, no-op.\n\nHowever, there's a wrinkle: `_discard_nonlinear_state_candidate(committed_states)` discards the ACTIVE trial. In the loop, the active trial is the current iteration's trial (at u). Discarding it before line search is safe because we only use `trial_states` (states_new) on convergence, which happens before delta computation.\n\nBut there's also the failure path: after max_iterations, `_discard_nonlinear_state_candidate(committed_states)` — discards whatever is active. If line search left the last trial discarded, nothing active → no-op. Fine.\n\nAlso `q_attempt_start`/rollback: q and lam are restored; states are restored because trials were never committed. Good.\n\nNow, where does the trial get created in _assemble_nonlinear_system? It calls begin_trial presumably (or replace_trial). If a trial is active when _assemble_nonlinear_system is called... In the current loop, each iteration calls _assemble_nonlinear_system while the previous iteration's trial is still active! How does that work? Let me check _assemble_nonlinear_system's trial handling — maybe it uses replace_trial (\"Reject any prior candidate and begin another\"). Let me check.", "summary": []}
