{"id": "reasoning-6dacc562-992b-5efe-a9a6-a6da9cd6239f-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349564527, "updatedAt": 1792349564527, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "`begin_state_evaluation` uses `replace_trial`, which rejects any prior candidate and begins another. So calling `_assemble_nonlinear_system` inside the loop for line-search evaluations is SAFE: it replaces the active trial automatically. The previous trial (this iteration's `trial_states`) is rejected — but on the delta path it was never going to be committed. And `states_new` is only set on the convergence path which breaks before delta.\n\nOne subtlety: after the line search, the loop continues to the next iteration, which calls _assemble_nonlinear_system → replace_trial again. Fine.\n\nBut careful about the convergence path: `states_new = trial_states; break` — then after the loop, commit happens. If the line search ran at iteration j and then iteration j+1 converges, states_new = trial_states of j+1 — correct.\n\nAnother subtlety: the line search happens after `q += delta[:-1]`? No — I'll do it before applying delta: compute merit at alpha candidates, pick alpha, then q += alpha*delta[:-1], lam += alpha*delta[-1]. \n\nNow, the merit at the current point: I have residual_norm (absolute), reference, constraint_error, target_scale from this iteration. merit_current = residual_norm/reference + constraint_error/target_scale.\n\nFor trial: need F_int at u_trial. Assemble with tangent=False (cheaper). For follower loads, F_ext depends on u: use _weighted_external_load_system(model, ..., u_trial, tangent=False). The EP case: follower_active False.\n\nImplementation sketch (inside the iteration loop, after delta computed and finite check, before contact admissible_step_fraction... wait, contact is None on the adaptive route, so the contact block is skipped anyway. Insert after the `if np.any(~np.isfinite(delta))` check, gated on `adaptive_control_subdivision`):\n\n```python\n                        if adaptive_control_subdivision:\n                            # Bounded residual line search (rotating-MPC,\n                            # contact-free route only): a full Newton step\n                            # can overshoot in the postyield regime.  Each\n                            # trial evaluation replaces the pending state\n                            # candidate and is never committed; committed\n                            # histories are retained by construction.\n                            merit_current = (\n                                residual_norm / reference\n                                + constraint_error / target_scale\n                            )\n                            line_search_alpha = 1.0\n                            if merit_current > 0.0 and np.any(delta):\n                                q_before = q.copy()\n                                lam_before = float(lam)\n                                for reduction in range(8):\n                                    alpha = 0.5 ** reduction\n                                    q_trial = q_before + alpha * delta[:-1]\n                                    lam_trial = lam_before + alpha * float(delta[-1])\n                                    u_trial = full_u(q_trial)\n                                    f_int_trial, _, _trial_states = (\n                                        _assemble_nonlinear_system(\n                                            model, u_trial, committed_states,\n                                            num_layers, tangent=False,\n                                            kinematics=kinematics,\n                                            corotational_tangent=corotational_tangent,\n                                        )\n                                    )\n                                    exact_guard(model, context=\"...\")\n                                    if follower_active:\n                                        f_const_trial, _ = _weighted_external_load_system(model, constant_terms, u_trial, tangent=False)\n                                        f_prop_trial, _ = _weighted_external_load_system(model, [proportional_term], u_trial, tangent=False)\n                                    else:\n                                        f_const_trial = F_const_static  # careful: F_const_current\n                                        f_prop_trial = F_prop_static\n                                    residual_trial = rotating_mpc_map.reduce_force(\n                                        u_trial,\n                                        f_const_trial + lam_trial * f_prop_trial - f_int_trial,\n                                    )\n                                    constraint_trial = abs(target - float(row_full @ u_trial))\n                                    merit_trial = (\n                                        float(np.linalg.norm(residual_trial)) / reference\n                                        + constraint_trial / target_scale\n                                    )\n                                    if merit_trial <= (1.0 - 1.0e-4 * alpha) * merit_current:\n                                        line_search_alpha = alpha\n                                        break\n                            delta *= line_search_alpha\n                            line_search_reductions_total += ... (record in info)\n```\n\nWait, but there's an issue: `merit_trial <= (1 - 1e-4*alpha)*merit_current` — for alpha=1 this requires sufficient decrease. If Newton is converging quadratically, merit at alpha=1 decreases a lot → accepted, no behavior change. If Newton overshoots, alpha=1 fails, backtrack.\n\nIf no alpha passes, keep alpha=1.0 (current behavior). Hmm — should we keep alpha=1 or use the best? Keep 1.0 to preserve existing behavior exactly when the line search can't find improvement.\n\nAlso record line-search usage in info: `info.setdefault(...)`? The DC info has \"displacement_control_adaptation\" — add \"line_search_reductions\" count there. Also maybe record per-step in history? Keep minimal: count total reductions (times alpha<1 accepted) in the adaptation info.\n\nNote: `delta *= line_search_alpha` scales both q and lam parts — the constraint row won't be satisfied exactly at alpha<1, but subsequent iterations continue Newton on the same target; convergence check requires both residual and constraint small, so the final accepted state satisfies both. Good.\n\nOne more consideration: the trial assemblies inside the line search each cost an assembly. With 8 reductions max per iteration and possibly many iterations... bounded. OK.\n\nAlso `exact_guard` calls: the loop uses exact_guard with contexts; I'll add one for the line-search assembly. Actually _assemble_nonlinear_system itself is guarded by callers; I'll add exact_guard after, matching the pattern.\n\nNow the lambda recovery. Where: in `_solve_static_displacement_control`, after `lam = float(initial_load_factor)` and after full_u/row_full are defined... it needs F_prop_static etc. which are defined at the top. And needs `reference`-like quantities. Implementation location: right after `row_full = displacement_control.full_row(model)` and the target_scale definition — need to see what's between line 3860 and 3930 (target, target_scale, row_red etc.). Let me read that region.", "summary": []}
