{"id": "reasoning-2cb0e12c-99f7-56fd-9d53-ee84587292dc-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349651365, "updatedAt": 1792349651365, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Excellent — highly discriminating evidence already recorded:\n- half[direct] PASSES including the 1e-6 wrench oracle at -0.10.\n- half[interp] fails ONLY the wrench balance: 12.8765 vs 61917 (2.08e-4 relative), while its reduced equilibrium residual passed 1e-7 (the assertion order: relative_residual <= 1e-7 came before the balance assert, so it passed).\n\nDirect (single master, w=1, exact rotation) passes the physical wrench; interp (two masters with distinct rotations, linearly averaged rotation vector) fails. This is consistent with cause (a): non-covariance of the weighted rotation-vector average. The competing cause (b) — a constituent work-map/recovery defect — would presumably affect direct too (same transfer machinery, same A matrices). Direct passing at 1e-6 strongly suggests the transfer/recovery machinery is sound and the interp-specific averaged orientation is responsible.\n\nBut the brief demands: \"Derive a discriminating global rigid-spin virtual-work/objectivity check before changing mechanics.\" So I still implement the rigid-spin equivariance check as a diagnostic (cheap) to directly demonstrate the kinematic non-equivariance for interp and equivariance for direct. That converts the circumstantial evidence into a direct discrimination.\n\nNow — the early checkpoint is overdue (turn ~20). Write it NOW with:\n1. Findings: DC1/DC2 fixed (edits applied, syntax-verified, not yet numerically verified); recorded evidence shows half[direct] passes wrench 1e-6 while half[interp] fails only the wrench (2.08e-4) with small reduced residual → interp-specific.\n2. Objectivity derivation + discriminating check design.\n3. SO(3) mean proposal with connected map/Jacobian/geometric tangent/covector treatment.\n4. Intended edits: line search, lambda recovery, D1 spy test, zero-span test, T2/T3/T4.\n5. Budget state: 0 additional seconds spent so far this assignment.\n\nThen continue implementation. Let me write the checkpoint update now (append an \"early checkpoint\" section, replacing the \"Status\" header appropriately). I'll rewrite checkpoint.md with the early-checkpoint section added.", "summary": []}
