": 1, \"lam\": 2.8162871515017565, \"iters\": 6, \"res\": 2.125268351160004e-06, \"ctrl\": -0.016666666666666666, \"eps_p\": 0.00020225943611388902}, {\"step\": 2, \"lam\": 4.920625200543552, \"iters\": 8, \"res\": 1.0955098031191376e-07, \"ctrl\": -0.03333333333333333, \"eps_p\": 0.0021070387643660642}, {\"step\": 3, \"lam\": 6.612279902029068, \"iters\": 8, \"res\": 1.6253738669437447e-05, \"ctrl\": -0.05000000000000001, \"eps_p\": 0.004098929751393017}, {\"step\": 4, \"lam\": 8.145093185589646, \"iters\": 8, \"res\": 1.5582440091592209e-07, \"ctrl\": -0.06666666666666667, \"eps_p\": 0.006135490816620431}, {\"step\": 5, \"lam\": 9.599335430165452, \"iters\": 7, \"res\": 7.771166700792632e-07, \"ctrl\": -0.08333333333333333, \"eps_p\": 0.00811264692404359}]}\r\n", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && ls evidence/ep-dc-limit-probe-1/ evidence/ep-dc-block-probe-direct-1/ 2>/dev/null && echo === && tail -40 evidence/ep-dc-limit-probe-1/stdout.txt", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-7cc3f8f9-7060-5d88-8918-650f1d535a21-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349671145, "updatedAt": 1792349671145, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Very informative. This probe was run BEFORE subdivision was implemented (fixed increments, no cutbacks): direct fails at step 11 (after 10 accepted steps to -.1667), interp fails at step 6 (after 5 accepted to -.0833). Each accepted step takes 6-8 iterations — that's already high for Newton with a consistent tangent (suggesting only linear convergence, i.e., a continuum/elastic-plastic tangent or the work_conjugate geometric approximation). With 40 max iterations and subdivision down to span/256, still failing → the Newton iteration is not converging at all near those states, or converging extremely slowly.\n\nNote the residuals at acceptance: 1e-7 to 1e-5 — wait, the convergence criterion is residual <= tol*reference = 1e-8 * reference. res 1.4e-5 (step 4) — that's the recorded residual_norm (absolute), reference must be ~1e3. OK.\n\nIterations 6-8 per step with tiny increments at the end — the pattern res ~1e-6..1e-5 at acceptance with 7 iterations suggests slow linear convergence (rate ~0.1-0.5?). If the convergence rate degrades near the stall point, 40 iterations may not be enough even for tiny increments. A residual line search won't fix linear convergence; it fixes divergence/oscillation.\n\nHmm, what does \"maximum_iterations_reached\" with subdivision look like? block-probe-direct-1: 14 accepts/26 attempts/11 cuts, terminal -.1833. So with subdivision, step 11 accepted 4 sub-increments (14 accepts vs 10 before) then failed at min step.\n\nWhat's the actual iteration behavior at the failing attempt? Let me check block-probe-direct-1 stdout for iteration-level detail.", "summary": []}
