{"id": "effect-6ea5526d-d2db-5758-af03-6c31ef50f2fe", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349736565, "updatedAt": 1792349736613, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "offset": 56, "limit": 120}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": "    \"Iz\": 0.04 * (0.01**3) / 12.0,\n    \"J\": 1.0e-8,\n}\n\n\ndef _build_coupled_cantilever(\n    route: str,\n    *,\n    nx: int = 2,\n    ny: int = 1,\n    length: float = 1.0,\n    width: float = 0.2,\n    thickness: float = 0.02,\n    eccentricity: tuple[float, float, float] = (0.0, 0.0, 0.05),\n    root_supports: bool = True,\n) -> tuple[FEModel, dict]:\n    \"\"\"Cantilever Q4 shell strip with a coupled eccentric beam stiffener.\"\"\"\n    model = FEModel(f\"slice3_{route}_{nx}x{ny}\")\n    model.add_material(\"steel\", 2.1e11, 0.3, density=7850.0)\n    r_vec = np.asarray(eccentricity, dtype=float)\n\n    grid: dict[tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n    node_id = 1\n    xs = np.linspace(0.0, length, nx + 1)\n    ys = np.linspace(-0.5 * width, 0.5 * width, ny + 1)\n    for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n            model.add_node(node_id, float(x), float(y), 0.0)\n            grid[(ix, iy)] = node_id\n            node_id += 1\n\n    elem_id = 1\n    for ix in range(nx):\n        for iy in range(ny):\n            model.add_element(\n                elem_id,\n                create_shell_element(\n                    elem_id,\n                    [\n                        grid[(ix, iy)],\n                        grid[(ix + 1, iy)],\n                        grid[(ix + 1, iy + 1)],\n                        grid[(ix, iy + 1)],\n                    ],\n                    \"steel\",\n                    thickness=thickness,\n                ),\n            )\n            elem_id += 1\n\n    beam_nodes: list[int] = []\n    couplings: list[dict] = []\n    if route == \"eccentric\":\n        for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n            master_id = grid[(ix, 0)]\n            b_id = 100 + ix\n            model.add_node(b_id, float(x), -0.5 * width, float(r_vec[2]))\n            beam_nodes.append(b_id)\n            mpc_id = 200 + ix\n            model.add_element(\n                mpc_id,\n                CoupledBeamShellElement(\n                    mpc_id, beam_node_id=b_id, shell_node_id=master_id,\n                    material_name=\"steel\", eccentricity=r_vec,\n                ),\n            )\n            couplings.append(\n                {\"slave\": b_id, \"masters\": [master_id],\n                 \"weights\": np.array([1.0]), \"r\": r_vec.copy()}\n            )\n    elif route == \"interpolated\":\n        weights = np.array([0.6, 0.4], dtype=float)\n        for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n            m1 = grid[(ix, 0)]\n            m2 = grid[(ix, ny)]\n            b_id = 100 + ix\n            model.add_node(b_id, float(x), 0.0, float(r_vec[2]))\n            beam_nodes.append(b_id)\n            mpc_id = 200 + ix\n            model.add_element(\n                mpc_id,\n                InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement(\n                    mpc_id, b_id, [m1, m2], weights, eccentricity=r_vec,\n                ),\n            )\n            couplings.append(\n                {\"slave\": b_id, \"masters\": [m1, m2],\n                 \"weights\": weights.copy(), \"r\": r_vec.copy()}\n            )\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown route {route!r}\")\n\n    for ix in range(nx):\n        model.add_element(\n            300 + ix,\n            BeamElement(300 + ix, [beam_nodes[ix], beam_nodes[ix + 1]],\n                       \"steel\", cross_section=dict(CROSS_SECTION)),\n        )\n\n    root_nodes = [grid[(0, iy)] for iy in range(ny + 1)]\n    if root_supports:\n        model.add_boundary_condition(\n            BoundaryCondition(\n                \"root\", root_nodes,\n                {name: 0.0 for name in (\"ux\", \"uy\", \"uz\", \"rx\", \"ry\", \"rz\")},\n            )\n        )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    meta = {\n        \"route\": route,\n        \"grid\": grid,\n        \"beam_nodes\": beam_nodes,\n        \"root_nodes\": root_nodes,\n        \"couplings\": couplings,\n        \"eccentricity\": r_vec,\n        \"nx\": nx,\n        \"ny\": ny,\n    }\n    return model, meta\n\n", "numLines": 120, "startLine": 56, "requestedOffset": 56, "requestedLimit": 120, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "120 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-4e8717cd-e2f1-5d78-9e41-c54484de15f0-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349738629, "updatedAt": 1792349738629, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Good — `_build_coupled_cantilever(\"eccentric\")` gives a small model. For the D1 spy test I need a small DC solve on the rotating route. Let me look at test_r5_finite_state_admits_nonlinear_only_control_and_load to see how they set up a small DC solve (lines 676-730).", "summary": []}
{"id": "effect-3166fcce-4960-596b-95f5-0fb576082b07", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349738653, "updatedAt": 1792349738698, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.read_file", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.read_file", "display": {"summary": "Reading C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Reading", "message": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "settledVerb": "Read", "settledMessage": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "statusText": "Reading file"}, "kind": "file_read", "input": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "offset": 635, "limit": 115}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"filePath": "C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "content": "    \"\"\"Root clamp plus fixed master uz; the tip beam slave uz is the control.\n\n    The linear MPC gives u_b,z = u_s,z (the lever arm (theta x r0)_z is zero\n    for r0 = (0, 0, e)), so with the master uz fixed the linear control row\n    vanishes.  The nonlinear position u_b,z = ... + (cos(ry) - 1) e has a\n    nonzero finite-state derivative -e sin(ry), so the same control coordinate\n    is usable at a finite-rotation restart.\n    \"\"\"\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\n        \"eccentric\", nx=2, ny=1, eccentricity=(0.0, 0.0, 0.05)\n    )\n    tip_master = meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)]\n    model.add_boundary_condition(\n        BoundaryCondition(\"fix_master_uz\", [tip_master], {\"uz\": 0.0})\n    )\n    model.apply_boundary_conditions()\n    pre_load = LoadCase(\"bending\")\n    pre_load.add_nodal_load(\n        meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], meta[\"ny\"])], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -1.0e5)\n    )\n    model.add_load_case(pre_load)\n    slave_load = LoadCase(\"slave_uz_load\")\n    slave_load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -5.0e3))\n    model.add_load_case(slave_load)\n    return model, meta, pre_load, slave_load\n\n\ndef test_r5_zero_jacobian_control_refused_at_zero_rotation() -> None:\n    model, meta, _pre_load, slave_load = _r5_model()\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"zero control Jacobian\"):\n        solve_static_nonlinear(\n            model, slave_load, control=\"displacement\",\n            displacement_control=control,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=20,\n            tolerance=1.0e-8,\n        )\n\n\ndef test_r5_finite_state_admits_nonlinear_only_control_and_load() -> None:\n    model, meta, pre_load, slave_load = _r5_model()\n    dofs = model.mesh.dof_manager.get_node_dofs\n\n    # Reach a genuine finite-rotation equilibrium with a dead shell load.\n    pre = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, pre_load, num_steps=6, max_iterations=25, tolerance=1.0e-9,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", corotational_tangent=\"auto\",\n    )\n    assert pre.converged\n    assert pre.status == \"completed\"\n    assert abs(float(pre.load_factor) - 1.0) <= 1.0e-12\n    pre_u = np.asarray(pre.displacements, dtype=float)\n    tip_master_ry = float(pre_u[dofs(meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)])[4]])\n    assert tip_master_ry != 0.0\n\n    # The regression is the admission itself, not a particular large angle:\n    # the control coordinate is nonlinear-only, so the linear row is exactly\n    # zero while the finite-state kinematic Jacobian row and the proportional\n    # load projection are both nonzero at this equilibrium (and both vanish\n    # at the zero-rotation origin, which the refusal test covers).\n    K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n    F_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, slave_load)\n    _, _, T, _u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\n    mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n    assert mpc_map is not None and mpc_map.active\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-0.01\n    )\n    row_full = control.full_row(model)\n    row_linear = np.asarray(row_full @ T, dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n    assert float(np.linalg.norm(row_linear)) == 0.0\n    row_finite = np.asarray(row_full @ mpc_map.jacobian(pre_u)).reshape(-1)\n    assert float(np.linalg.norm(row_finite)) > 0.0\n    zero_u = np.zeros_like(pre_u)\n    assert float(np.linalg.norm(mpc_map.reduce_force(zero_u, F_prop))) == 0.0\n    assert float(np.linalg.norm(mpc_map.reduce_force(pre_u, F_prop))) > 0.0\n\n    # Controlled increment near that state: the presolved equilibrium is held\n    # by the same dead load as a constant load case, so the displacement-\n    # control unknown only carries the slave-only proportional load and the\n    # initial state is an exact equilibrium of the restarted system.\n    initial_control = float(row_full @ pre_u)\n    target = initial_control - 8.0e-6\n    control_increment = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=float(target)\n    )\n    u_input = np.array(pre_u, dtype=float, copy=True)\n    states_input = copy.deepcopy(dict(pre.element_states))\n    u_snapshot = np.array(pre_u, dtype=float, copy=True)\n    states_snapshot = copy.deepcopy(dict(pre.element_states))\n    result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, slave_load, constant_load_case=pre_load,\n        control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control_increment,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=30,\n        tolerance=1.0e-8, initial_displacements=u_input,\n        initial_element_states=states_input,\n        equilibrate_initial_state=False,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    # Caller-supplied restart inputs are preserved by the solve.\n    np.testing.assert_array_equal(u_input, u_snapshot)\n    _assert_element_states_equal(states_input, states_snapshot)\n    uz = float(result.displacements[dofs(meta[\"beam_nodes\"][-1])[2]])\n    assert abs(uz - target) <= 1.0e-8\n    assert abs(float(result.load_factor)) > 0.0\n    # The accepted control motion is carried by the nonlinear map: the fixed\n    # master translation stays exactly zero while the master rotation vector\n    # changes enough to move the slave through the finite-rotation lever arm.\n    master_dofs = dofs(meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)])\n    assert float(result.displacements[master_dofs[2]]) == 0.0\n    theta_change = float(np.linalg.norm(\n        np.asarray(result.displacements[master_dofs[3:6]], dtype=float)\n        - pre_u[master_dofs[3:6]]\n", "numLines": 115, "startLine": 635, "requestedOffset": 635, "requestedLimit": 115, "totalLines": null, "wasTruncated": true}, "outputText": "", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Read", "message": "115 lines from C:\\Github\\ANYsolver\\tests\\test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": "(truncated)"}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "reasoning-cadcb82d-40eb-5bd6-a418-386d297e2440-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349755602, "updatedAt": 1792349755602, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "I have the pattern. Now write the D1 spy test. Design:\n\n```python\ndef test_d1_displacement_control_augmented_factorization_declared_general(monkeypatch) -> None:\n    \"\"\"D1: the assembled augmented DC system must be declared MatrixClass.GENERAL...\"\"\"\n    import anysolver.nonlinear_static as nonlinear_static\n    from anysolver.linalg import MatrixClass\n\n    model, meta = _build_coupled_cantilever(\"eccentric\")\n    load = LoadCase(\"tip\")\n    load.add_nodal_load(meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], meta[\"ny\"])], forces=(0.0, 0.0, -1.0e4))\n    model.add_load_case(load)\n    control = DisplacementControl(\n        node_id=meta[\"grid\"][(meta[\"nx\"], 0)], dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=-1.0e-3\n    )\n\n    recorded: list = []\n    real_factorize = nonlinear_static.factorize\n\n    def spy(matrix, matrix_class, **kwargs):\n        recorded.append(matrix_class)\n        return real_factorize(matrix, matrix_class, **kwargs)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(nonlinear_static, \"factorize\", spy)\n    result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n        model, load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n        kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=2, max_iterations=20,\n        tolerance=1.0e-8,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"completed\"\n    assert recorded, \"no factorization was observed on the DC route\"\n    assert all(mc is MatrixClass.GENERAL for mc in recorded)\n```\n\nWait — is `factorize` called elsewhere in the same solve with other classes (e.g., the initial linear solve for constraint transformation)? build_constraint_transformation may factorize with another class (SYMMETRIC). The spy records ALL calls during the solve; asserting all GENERAL could fail if some other legitimate factorization (e.g., linear stiffness for T) uses a different class. The DC-specific assertion: the augmented path's calls are GENERAL. To discriminate, filter by matrix shape: the augmented matrix has the extra row/col (n_red+1). Simpler: assert that at least one GENERAL call occurred AND no call on an (n+1)-shaped augmented matrix used a non-GENERAL class. Even simpler and robust: record (shape, class) and assert every recorded matrix whose shape is (n_red+1, n_red+1)... I don't know n_red in the test easily — I can compute T. Alternative: assert all recorded classes are GENERAL — but the pre-solve/linear admission factorizations might use SYMMETRIC. Hmm.\n\nCleanest: record classes ONLY for matrices whose shape is square with odd... no. Let me record (shape, class) and assert: every factorization of a matrix with shape (k+1, k+1) where... I can get n_red from build_constraint_transformation like other tests do. The augmented matrix is (n_red+1, n_red+1). Other factorizations (linear stiffness) are (total_dofs, total_dofs) or (n_red, n_red). So:\n\n```python\nK0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\nF_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load)\n_, _, T, _u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\nn_red = T.shape[1]\naug_calls = [cls for shape, cls in recorded if shape == (n_red + 1, n_red + 1)]\nassert aug_calls\nassert all(cls is MatrixClass.GENERAL for cls in aug_calls)\n```\n\nAnd also assert the solve completed (delegation unchanged). This is PARDISO-independent: the spy delegates to the real factorize whatever backend is configured.\n\nAlso should the spy verify the augmented matrix is actually nonsymmetric? Not needed — D1 is about the declared class.\n\nWhere to add: tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3.py (source-regression module). The module currently has 16 passes; adding this test changes it → rerunning permitted (as \"changed source\" module).\n\nWait — does the small elastic DC solve on this fixture work? test_r5 shows DC on this model works (with restart). A fresh DC from zero: control = tip shell node uz, target -1e-3, 2 steps, elastic (no plasticity in this fixture — material has no hardening curve → elastic). Should complete quickly (~1-3 s with NUMBA_DISABLE_JIT? These small tests: the slice3 module's 16 tests took 40s total).\n\nNow the continuation module edits (zero-span + T2/T3/T4). Let me write them.\n\n**T2**: parameterize _independent_equilibrium over an explicit state. Refactor:\n\n```python\ndef _independent_equilibrium(case, *, displacements=None, lam=None, states=None) -> dict:\n    u = np.asarray(case[\"result\"].displacements if displacements is None else displacements, float)\n    lam = float(case[\"result\"].load_factor if lam is None else lam)\n    states = case[\"result\"].element_states if states is None else states\n    states = copy.deepcopy(dict(states))\n    ...\n    reference = mpc_map.reduce_force(u, lam * F_prop)  # achieved-load normalization\n    relative = norm(reduced)/max(norm(reference), 1.0)\n```\n\nWait the review: \"The helper currently divides by norm(J.T F_prop), not norm(J.T lambda*F_prop). For an achieved-load relative-residual claim use max(norm(J.T F_actual),1)\". So change reference to lam*F_prop reduced. This makes the criterion stricter for lam>1... For direct full at lam~2.7: reference becomes 2.7x larger → relative residual smaller → still passes 1e-7? The recorded passes had relative <= 1e-7 with the unit-load normalization; with lam normalization the value shrinks by ~2.7 → still passes. For early snapshots lam<1 the criterion is stricter. Fine — it's the adopted definition.\n\nThen in _assert_completed_dc_case, add per-snapshot checks:\n\n```python\n    snapshots = result.snapshots\n    assert snapshots, \"completed DC case must record accepted snapshots\"\n    for snap in snapshots:\n        snap_u = np.asarray(snap.displacements, dtype=float)\n        snap_states = copy.deepcopy(dict(snap.el