element: plastic_strain tensors, alpha arrays, fiber histories — i.e., compare the full element_states dicts with _assert_states_equal? Exact equality is too strict (different Newton paths give roundoff differences). Use allclose with existing tolerances (rtol 1e-6, atol 1e-9). Need a recursive allclose comparator for state dicts with arrays. The states contain dicts of arrays (plastic_strain, alpha, fiber histories...). Write `_assert_states_allclose(left, right)` recursive: arrays → assert_allclose(rtol=1e-6, atol=1e-9); scalars → ==... hmm floats: allclose too. But some state entries may be non-numeric (strings/ints for IDs) → equality.\n\nAlso \"Compare the half-run prefix with the uninterrupted prefix too\": half snapshots at milestones -1/6..-5/6*0.10... half milestones: -0.10* k/6 for k=1..6 vs full at same control values (full milestones at -0.20*k/12 = -0.10*k/6 — same grid!). So compare half snapshots vs full snapshots at all 6 common milestones.\n\n**T4**: \n- rejected test: add states deep copy + compare after refusal.\n- stopped test: compare returned displacements/element states with last accepted snapshot or half input.\n- cancelled test: freeze half snapshots before, compare after; capture _increment_snapshot outputs via monkeypatch to observe snapshots accepted before cancellation; verify they retain accepted history.\n\nFor the capture: monkeypatch `anysolver.nonlinear_static._increment_snapshot`? The function references it module-locally: `snapshots.append(_increment_snapshot(...))` — monkeypatching the module attribute works since it's looked up at call time (module global). Signature: _increment_snapshot(record_step_index, lam, u, committed_states, control_value=...) — let me check its signature.\n\nLet me check _increment_snapshot and NonlinearIncrementSnapshot fields.", "summary": []}
