{"id": "reasoning-6e42fff5-13b2-5d06-afe9-c25b64d1b063-0", "sessionId": "01f7c834-c499-fb2f-0e3f-33d4d208c428", "turnId": "turn-d4c99f7f7fae63d9ba666324f5523e64", "createdAt": 1792349770869, "updatedAt": 1792349770869, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "D1 test added. Now the continuation module edits. These are more extensive. Let me do them with the edit tool (LF file). I'll make the edits one at a time.\n\n**Edit 1: refactor _independent_equilibrium** to accept explicit state and use achieved-load normalization + oracle caching.\n\nCurrent function (lines 307-376). I'll replace the signature and body parts. New version:\n\n```python\ndef _equilibrium_oracle(case: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Cached assembly/map context for independent equilibrium checks.\"\"\"\n    if \"_oracle\" not in case:\n        model, load = case[\"model\"], case[\"load\"]\n        K0, _ = assemble_stiffness_matrix(model)\n        F_prop, _ = assemble_load_vector(model, load)\n        _, _, T, _u0, _, _ = build_constraint_transformation(K0, F_prop, model)\n        mpc_map = build_nonlinear_rotating_mpc_map(model, T)\n        assert mpc_map is not None and mpc_map.active\n        case[\"_oracle\"] = {\"mpc_map\": mpc_map, \"F_prop\": np.asarray(F_prop, dtype=float)}\n    return case[\"_oracle\"]\n\n\ndef _independent_equilibrium(case: dict, *, displacements=None, load_factor=None, element_states=None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Residual at the achieved load factor plus explicit force/wrench balance.\n\n    ... (docstring update)\n    \"\"\"\n    oracle = _equilibrium_oracle(case)\n    mpc_map = oracle[\"mpc_map\"]\n    F_prop = oracle[\"F_prop\"]\n    model = case[\"model\"]\n    grid = case[\"grid\"]\n    result = case[\"result\"]\n    u = (np.asarray(result.displacements, dtype=float) if displacements is None\n         else np.asarray(displacements, dtype=float))\n    lam = float(result.load_factor if load_factor is None else load_factor)\n    sta